       "content": "# Research Agenda: Reducing Hallucinated Citations in LLM Outputs\n\n## Experiment 1: Systematic Failure Mode Taxonomy\n\n**Hypothesis:** Hallucinated citations are not a monolithic failure mode. They cluster into distinct categories (fabricated papers, real papers with wrong claims, real papers with wrong metadata, plausible-but-false authorship) that are triggered by different conditions and require different interventions.\n\n**Dataset construction:**\n- Build a benchmark of ~5,",
       "name": null,
